    {
      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To solve the problem, we first identify the sequence in question. The sequence is defined as follows:\n\n\\[ T_n = 3^0 + 3^1 + 3^2 + \\cdots + 3^{n-1} \\]\n\nwhere \\( T_n \\) is the sum of the first \\( n \\) terms of the geometric series with the first term \\( a = 1 \\) and common ratio \\( r = 3 \\). Thus, the \\( n \\)-th term of the sequence is:\n\n\\[ T_n = 3^n - 1 \\]\n\nWe need to find the value of the fourth term of the sequence, which corresponds to \\( n = 4 \\). Substituting \\( n = 4 \\) into the formula for the \\( n \\)-th term, we get:\n\n\\[ T_4 = 3^4 - 1 \\]\n\nNext, we calculate \\( 3^4 \\):\n\n\\[ 3^4 = 3 \\times 3 \\times 3 \\times 3 = 81 \\]\n\nTherefore,\n\n\\[ T_4 = 81 - 1 = 80 \\]\n\nSo, the simplified value of the fourth term of the sequence is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{80}\n\\]",
